{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792870189,"nonce":"4mhBCULTmDfgaOq5o3ZLwkEKDn0=","title":"Keep Jam controls reactive after session restore and show extension loading feedback","message":"The user ended a Jam, closed RayDE and reopened it. The Jam panel showed the restored filename but Start, Join, Resume and Rejoin were disabled; switching tabs eventually made them usable. JamPanel passes one-time Bool snapshots to reactive-capable Button.disabled props, while text interpolation keeps following active changes. Fix idle and live Jam button eligibility bindings and cover active-tab restoration, switching to unsupported tabs and returning, leaving a room and asynchronous session readiness.\n\nThe user also requests explicit loading feedback whenever an extension is not ready. Cover extension startup/activation and views or commands awaiting registration; clear feedback when ready, stopped, failed or disposed. Do not treat Jam's stale disabled bindings as an extension-startup delay, or block the UI to wait for readiness.\n\nRelated Jam integration: ae67eb4c47e1dd805a71779ac1799446d46280be4ad569395bf806bbb552cd79","files":null}]}